      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|2|=2$ centered at the point $(2,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/05996c6895718404008ed930e4410d7f410f946568721b06736bd7915afa88ba.png)",
